    "answer": "I mapped the 10 distribution centers and checked the screenshot. **All 10 points show up, and each one is where it should be relative to the others.**\n\nWhat the screenshot shows:\n- **Far west, on its own:** Los Angeles, CA.\n- **Midwest / middle South:** Chicago, IL at the top and Memphis, TN below it.\n- **Gulf Coast, along the bottom:** Houston, TX, then New Orleans, LA, then Mobile, AL, from west to east.\n- **Southeast Atlantic coast:** Charleston, SC, with Savannah, GA just south and west of it.\n- **Northeast, top right:** Port Authority NY/NJ, with Philadelphia, PA just below it.\n\nNine of the 10 centers are east of the Mississippi or on the Gulf Coast; Los Angeles is the only one in the west.\n\nTwo things to know about the map:\n- **There's no basemap.** It shows only the points and their labels, with no state or country outlines. The map tool can't load outline files from the web, so the check is based on how the points sit relative to each other, which matches real US geography.\n- **The map zooms to fit the points.** Los Angeles sits at the left edge and NY/NJ at the right, so the frame covers only the area the centers span, not the whole US."
